James announced the release of his new publication, "Comprehensive national climate damage assessments framework applied to the UK," in *Nature Climate Change*, co-authored with several researchers. He requested assistance in crafting social media posts, an HTML block for his lab website, and a professional blog article. In response, concise summaries were created tailored for Fediscience/X and LinkedIn, highlighting the study’s key findings such as the estimation of climate-related welfare losses in the UK at 2% of GDP currently, rising to ~10% by the century's end under a high-emissions scenario. The HTML block was formatted for his website, and a blog post articulated the motivation and methodologies underlying the research, emphasizing the aim of providing a comprehensive assessment of national climate damages.
